  * (vendor dsi_ctrl_hw_cmn_kickoff_fifo_command): header dword [wc_lo wc_hi data_type flags], payload,
  * flags bit 7 the last command, bit 6 a payload follows. The controller is the first of ctrl0/ctrl1 that
  * completes a command.
+ *
+ * And the panel's own frame signal: the boot loader runs INTF1's tear check on the panel's TE pin
+ * (SYNC_CONFIG_VSYNC 0x180088: hw vsync mode, counter on, 136 vsync-clock ticks a line) with
+ * autorefresh every TE, so the panel's refresh is the panel's, not ours. sweet_panel_te() reads when
+ * the last TE came from the tear check's read pointer (loaded with VSYNC_INIT_VAL at a TE, then one up
+ * per line) and how many have come. kern.sweet_mdss reads and writes the display block's registers
+ * (MDSS, the DSI controllers, PHYs and PLLs, the display clock controller) and sends the panel DCS
+ * writes: what tools/mdss (userland/mdss.c) measures and tries the panel's refresh rate with.
  */
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_RAPHAEL)
 #include <sys/param.h>
 #include <sys/systm.h>
